    <header class="mb-10">
      <div class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-wider text-blue-400 uppercase mb-3">Corporate Tax Architecture • Micro-SaaS Structuring</div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white mb-6 leading-tight">
        Estonia e-Residency Corporate Tax Deferral: 0% Tax on Reinvested SaaS Profits (2026)
      </h1>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        An exhaustive architectural guide to establishing an Estonian OÜ, maximizing corporate reinvestment compound growth, navigating dividend distribution mathematics, and mitigating Permanent Establishment (PE) risks.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Google Quick Answer Callout -->
    <div class="bg-slate-900/80 border-l-4 border-blue-500 rounded-xl p-6 mb-10 shadow-lg backdrop-blur-sm">
      <div class="text-xs uppercase font-bold text-blue-400 mb-2">Google Quick Answer</div>
      <p class="text-base text-slate-200 leading-relaxed font-medium">
        <strong>Estonia’s corporate tax regime levies 0% corporate income tax on retained and reinvested business profits.</strong> For bootstrapped SaaS founders, this unique structure allows 100% of top-line software revenue to compound tax-free into server hosting, AI inference APIs, hardware, and growth marketing. Taxes are deferred entirely until dividends are distributed, at which point a flat <strong>20/80 rate (25% effective on net)</strong> applies to distributed capital.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="prose prose-invert max-w-none space-y-8">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">1. The Unique Mechanics of the Estonian Corporate Income Tax Model</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          In virtually all traditional OECD jurisdictions (the United States, United Kingdom, Germany, France), corporate income tax is assessed annually on net accounting profit. If your Micro-SaaS generates $200,000 in gross revenue and incurs $50,000 in operational expenses, you are taxed on the remaining $150,000 profit at rates between 19% and 30%, whether or not you take money out of the business.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          Estonia operates on a completely different philosophical principle under Chapter 10 of the Estonian Income Tax Act (*Tulumaksuseadus*):
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-300">
          <li><strong>0% Annual Corporate Income Tax:</strong> Retained profits kept in corporate bank accounts, treasury bills, money market funds, or reinvested in corporate expansion trigger zero annual tax liability.</li>
          <li><strong>Distribution-Based Taxation:</strong> Tax liability is deferred indefinitely until value leaves the corporate veil via dividends, share buybacks, or non-business expense distributions.</li>
          <li><strong>Zero Annual Filing Friction:</strong> Corporate tax returns (TSD form) are filed monthly only if distributions or fringe benefits occurred; otherwise, filing takes seconds via Estonia's digitized e-Tax portal.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">2. Reinvestment Compound Growth: Estonia OÜ vs US LLC vs UK Ltd</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          To illustrate the power of tax deferral, consider a bootstrapped SaaS venture generating $150,000 in annual net earnings, compounding at 25% growth over a 5-year reinvestment horizon before founder liquidation.
        </p>

        <!-- Compound Growth Table -->
        <div class="overflow-x-auto my-6">
          <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse border border-slate-700 text-sm">
            <thead>
              <tr class="bg-slate-950 text-slate-200">
                <th class="p-3 border border-slate-700">Jurisdiction & Corporate Entity</th>
                <th class="p-3 border border-slate-700">Annual Corporate Tax Rate</th>
                <th class="p-3 border border-slate-700">Year 3 Reinvestment Pool</th>
                <th class="p-3 border border-slate-700">Year 5 Corporate Treasury Balance</th>
                <th class="p-3 border border-slate-700 text-blue-400 font-bold">5-Year Growth Advantage</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 text-slate-300">
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">United States (C-Corp)</td>
                <td class="p-3">21% Federal + ~7% State</td>
                <td class="p-3">$325,400</td>
                <td class="p-3">$742,000</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-slate-400">Baseline</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">United Kingdom (Ltd)</td>
                <td class="p-3">25% Corporation Tax</td>
                <td class="p-3">$338,200</td>
                <td class="p-3">$774,500</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-slate-400">+4.3%</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Germany (GmbH)</td>
