                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-blue-300 font-bold">Estonia (OÜ via e-Residency)</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-emerald-400 font-bold">0.0% (Reinvested)</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-emerald-400 font-bold">$457,800</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-emerald-400 font-bold">$1,072,500</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-emerald-400 font-bold">+$330,500 (+44.5%)</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">3. Mathematical Derivation of the 20/80 Dividend Formula</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          A common point of confusion among founders is how Estonia calculates corporate tax upon dividend distribution. Under the Estonian tax code, the tax is structured as 20% on the gross distribution amount (<code>D_gross</code>), which equates to the 20/80 formula applied to net dividend payout (<code>D_net</code>):
        </p>

        <div class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 p-5 rounded-xl my-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 mb-2">Mathematical Dividend Tax Formula:</p>
          <code class="text-lg font-mono text-blue-400">Tax = Net Dividend × (20 / 80) = Net Dividend × 0.25</code>
        </div>

        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          <strong>Concrete Calculation Example:</strong> If your Estonian OÜ decides to distribute €100,000 net into your personal bank account:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 text-slate-300">
          <li><strong>Net Payout to Founder:</strong> €100,000.00</li>
          <li><strong>Estonian Tax Remittance:</strong> €100,000 × (20 / 80) = <strong>€25,000.00</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Total Corporate Outflow:</strong> €125,000.00 (Gross Distribution)</li>
          <li><strong>Verification:</strong> €25,000 tax ÷ €125,000 gross = Exactly 20.00%</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">4. Banking & Payment Processing Setup: Wise, LHV, and Polar.sh</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          Operating an Estonian OÜ remotely without traveling to Tallinn is fully supported by modern European digital banking infrastructure:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-slate-300">
          <li class="bg-slate-900/50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-800">
            <strong class="text-white text-base">Wise Business (formerly TransferWise):</strong> Can be opened 100% online in less than 48 hours using your e-Residency digital ID card. Provides dedicated EUR IBANs, multi-currency balances (USD, GBP, JPY), and low-cost SEPA/SWIFT wire routing.
          </li>
          <li class="bg-slate-900/50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-800">
            <strong class="text-white text-base">LHV Pank:</strong> A premier Estonian tech-focused bank offering dedicated startup accounts. While traditionally requiring one physical in-person branch verification in Tallinn, LHV now permits remote video KYC for qualified e-residents working with authorized corporate service providers (e.g., Xolo, Companio).
          </li>
          <li class="bg-slate-900/50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-800">
            <strong class="text-white text-base">Merchant of Record Integration:</strong> Link your Estonian OÜ directly to Polar.sh or Lemon Squeezy to automate cross-border global VAT remittance and credit card processing.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">5. Managing Permanent Establishment (PE) & Place of Effective Management Risks</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          The single greatest legal mistake foreign founders make with an Estonian OÜ is ignoring **Permanent Establishment (PE)** and **Place of Effective Management (POEM)** rules defined by OECD Model Tax Convention Article 5:
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          If you reside physically in high-tax countries like France, Spain, or Germany and make all executive corporate decisions from your living room, the local tax authorities may deem your Estonian OÜ to possess a local Permanent Establishment, taxing the company's profits under local domestic corporate tax laws.
        </p>
        <div class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-5 text-slate-300 space-y-2">
          <p class="font-semibold text-white">How Digital Nomads Legally Protect Their Estonian OÜ:</p>
          <p>1. <strong>Maintain Nomad Tax Status:</strong> Spend less than 183 days in any single country and avoid establishing a permanent home or center of vital economic interests in restrictive tax jurisdictions.</p>
          <p>2. <strong>Pair with Low-Tax Residency:</strong> Combine your Estonian OÜ with personal tax residency in territorial tax or zero-foreign-income jurisdictions (e.g., Cyprus Non-Dom, Malta Nomad Residence, Paraguay, Panama, or UAE).</p>
          <p>3. <strong>Document Estonian Substance:</strong> Utilize an Estonian authorized legal contact person, virtual office address, and engage local accounting services in Tallinn.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">6. Summary Checklist for Incorporating via e-Residency</h2>
        <div class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6 text-slate-300 space-y-3">
          <p class="font-semibold text-white">Step-by-Step Incorporation Pipeline:</p>
          <p>1. Apply online for Estonian e-Residency at `e-resident.gov.ee` (€120 state fee); pick up digital ID kit at your nearest Estonian embassy.</p>
          <p>2. Engage an authorized corporate provider (Xolo Leap, Companio, or 1Office) for legal address and contact person service.</p>
          <p>3. Register your private limited company (*Osaühing* - OÜ) digitally in the Estonian Company Registration Portal in less than 2 hours (€265 state fee).</p>
          <p>4. Open an EU business account with Wise Business or Revolut Business using your digital signature certificate.</p>
          <p>5. Reinvest 100% of SaaS earnings into growth, APIs, and infrastructure with zero annual corporate tax drag.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
